### 2. Give each spec its own account

`storageState` reuses authentication; it does not isolate server-side user settings. Provision a unique picker account per test and create that test’s storage state from it. Adapt the account and login helpers to your app.

```ts
import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test';

export const test = base.extend({
  storageState: async ({ browser }, use, testInfo) => {
    const account = await createPickerAccount(randomUUID());

    try {
      const context = await browser.newContext();
      const page = await context.newPage();

      await login(page, account);

      const statePath = testInfo.outputPath('storage-state.json');
      await context.storageState({ path: statePath });
      await context.close();

      await use(statePath);
    } finally {
      await deletePickerAccount(account);
    }
  },
});
```

This lets the specs remain `fullyParallel`; each gets a separate user whose language changes cannot race with another spec’s. If provisioning an account per test isn’t practical, use a separate account per worker and reset its language before each test.

